  // Rule descriptions
  "carpet.rule.TotemWrench.desc": "Hold a totem of undying to rotate blocks: right-click with it in the main hand to rotate the targeted block, or keep it in the off hand to invert block placement.",

  "carpet.rule.InventoryTotem.desc": "A totem of undying in your inventory still protects you from death.",

  "carpet.rule.AccurateBlockPlacement.desc": "Client can provide alternative block placement.",

  "carpet.rule.CommandPing.desc": "Enables /ping command to check your latency.",

  "carpet.rule.FastLeafDecay.desc": "Leaves of a tree decay layer by layer within a few seconds once its log is broken.",

  "carpet.rule.EmeraldTemptsVillagers.desc": "Villagers are attracted to players holding an emerald.",

  "carpet.rule.DaytimeSleep.desc": "Players can sleep during the day, skipping time to nightfall.",

  "carpet.rule.QuickPaintingSwap.desc": "Sneak and right-click a placed painting to cycle it to another painting of the same size.",

  "carpet.rule.McdrCommandBridge.desc": "Enables /!! so MCDR commands are run as a command instead of being typed into chat.",

  "carpet.rule.ChatHeldItem.desc": "A # in chat is replaced by your held item: its icon when the mod is also on the client, its name otherwise.",

  "carpet.rule.SkipCommandConfirm.desc": "Commands that need elevated permissions run without the client-side confirmation dialog.",

  "carpet.rule.RightClickHarvest.desc": "Right-click a grown crop with an empty hand or with crops or seeds to harvest it and replant.",

  "carpet.rule.NoFarmlandTrample.desc": "Players no longer turn farmland into dirt by falling on it. false turns it off, true never breaks it, and a number allows that many tramples of one block before it breaks.",

  "carpet.rule.NoFarmlandTrampleScope.desc": "Who is protected: players keeps only player landings from breaking farmland, all protects every entity. Only meaningful while the trample rule is on.",

  "carpet.rule.DeathCoordinates.desc": "Announces where a player died, either to that player only or to everyone.",

  "carpet.rule.AfkMarker.desc": "Players who have neither moved nor turned for five minutes get an [AFK] name prefix.",

  "carpet.rule.AlwaysUnlockedRecipes.desc": "Unlocks every recipe when a player joins; recipes already unlocked are kept as they are.",

  "carpet.rule.BundleAutoEat.desc": "Eats one item from a bundle of food when hunger is low and that single item fills the bar (survival only). off disables it, saturation eats the lowest saturation first, slot follows the bundle order; food with its own effects always comes last.",

  "carpet.rule.FastEating.desc": "Caps eating and drinking time: false turns it off, true means 8 ticks, or pick 4 / 8 / 16 ticks directly. Items that are already faster keep their own time; the hunger check and item effects are unchanged.",

  "carpet.rule.TradePreview.desc": "Trade preview: the backpack lists every item the villager will ever sell, and the header becomes All trades.",

  "carpet.rule.FletchingTable.desc": "Right-click a fletching table to craft arrows; the two slots only take arrows and arrow materials, and the result follows the vanilla recipes. Needs the mod on both sides.",

  "carpet.rule.VillagerBackpack.desc": "Sneak and right-click a villager to open its backpack: a named villager always works, and a villager boxed into a single block works too. In the 9x6 screen the chest column holds its eight slots, the ender chest column lists the trades (paged, duplicates merged), the middle column shows profession, level and price situation, and the barrier closes it.",

  "carpet.rule.VehicleFireworkBoost.desc": "Using a firework rocket while riding a boat or minecart pushes it along your look direction; higher levels push harder.",

  "carpet.rule.VehicleInstantStop.desc": "A boat or minecart stops as soon as its rider leaves. all covers both, or pick minecart / boat only.",

  "carpet.rule.HappyGhastBoost.desc": "Using a firework rocket while riding a happy ghast dashes it along its current direction; higher levels dash further.",

